.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="For N_2O_4 \rightleftharpoons 2NO_2 the reaction quotient Q = x_{NO_2}^2/x_{N_2O_4} (at P = P^\circ), computed by reaction_quotient, rises monotonically with the extent of reaction. The law of mass action says the mixture stops changing where Q reaches the equilibrium constant K. Starting from different mixtures of reactant and product, the equilibrium compositions found by solve_equilibrium_composition all give the same Q = K.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/thermo/equilibrium/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_01_law_of_mass_action_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/thermo/equilibrium/plot_01_law_of_mass_action`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">Guldberg and Waage's law of mass action: Q = K at equilibrium</div>
    </div>


.. only:: not html

 * :doc:`/api/gallery/thermo/equilibrium/plot_01_law_of_mass_action`

.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Gibbs showed that at fixed temperature and pressure a system reaches equilibrium at the minimum of its total Gibbs energy G = \sum_i n_i\mu_i. For N_2O_4 \rightleftharpoons 2NO_2 this example plots G(\xi) from gibbs_energy_of_mixture at several temperatures and marks the composition returned by solve_equilibrium_composition, which sits at each minimum. The slope dG/d\xi = \sum_i\nu_i\mu_i (the reaction Gibbs energy) crosses zero there.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/thermo/equilibrium/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_02_gibbs_energy_minimization_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/thermo/equilibrium/plot_02_gibbs_energy_minimization`

